==============================================================================
A. CALIBRATION AGAINST `97`'S PUBLISHED COUNTS, ON `97`'S MODEL
==============================================================================
  6 regions, 5 arms, 2 coordinates (median algo_ns, bits per element)
  sections total                          15625
  rationalisable, w >= 0    this probe:       72    97 and 98 report      72
  rationalisable, w  > 0    this probe:        9    97 and 98 report       9
  instrument agrees with theirs: True

  Two exact implementations written from different geometries agreeing
  on both counts is a third instance of the same number. `98` was the
  second and wrote its own; this is written from interval and polygon
  clipping without reading either.

==============================================================================
B. THE CEILING AS A FUNCTION OF THE COORDINATE SET
==============================================================================
  How many sections a strictly positive weighting can reach. That is the
  number of distinguishable strategies the coordinate set supports; two
  weightings reaching the same section are the same strategy.

  coordinates                       arms  sections   w >= 0   w > 0
  {time}                               5     15625        1       1
  {time, size}                         5     15625       72       9
  {time, spread}                       5     15625        6       6
  {time, size, spread}                 5     15625      101      42
  {time}                               6     46656        1       1
  {time, size}                         6     46656       72       9
  {time, spread}                       6     46656       10      10
  {time, size, spread}                 6     46656      117      58

==============================================================================
C. WHAT THAT SAYS ABOUT A COORDINATE THAT DOES NOT EXIST
==============================================================================
  With one coordinate the weighting is a positive scalar, it cancels, and
  exactly one section is reachable: every strategy agrees, by algebra and
  not by luck. Each coordinate added multiplies what the space can express.

  So a strategy whose intent names a quantity with no coordinate is not
  merely unmeasured. It is INEXPRESSIBLE: there is no axis along which it
  can differ from any other strategy, so it and its opposite are the same
  point in the space, whatever the canon calls them.
